cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI Value Lab: evidence driven AI use case assessment"
message: "If you reference this methodology, its metrics, or its outputs, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Raghuveeran"
    given-names: "Preethi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pretzelslab/ai-value-lab"
abstract: >-
  An assessment toolkit that connects the economic case for an AI use case to
  measured evidence about how the system behaves. It converts evaluation
  evidence into a measured control effectiveness, carries the resulting
  residual risk into the business case, and reports what each point of risk
  removed costs. Outputs a routing rule through a workflow rather than a
  single verdict on it, with a provenance tag and an interval on every
  material number.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - responsible AI
  - AI assurance
  - control effectiveness
  - evaluation design
  - residual risk
  - AI business case
  - decision traceability
